 "annotations": [
  {
   "text": "On September 14th, the price of U. S. Steel was recorded in the Downward Trend column. Refer to Explanatory Rule 5-B.",
   "ruleRefs": [
    "5-B"
   ],
   "dateRefs": [
    "1938-09-14"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "On the same day a price was recorded in the Natural Reaction column of Bethlehem Steel. That price was still being recorded in the Natural Reaction column because it had not reached a price that was 3 points lower than its previous price with red lines drawn.",
   "dateRefs": [
    "1938-09-14"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "On September 20th, prices of U. S. Steel and Bethlehem Steel were recorded in the Natural Rally column. Refer to Explanatory Rule 6-C for U. S. Steel and 6-D for Bethlehem Steel.",
   "ruleRefs": [
    "6-C",
    "6-D"
   ],
   "dateRefs": [
    "1938-09-20"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "On September 24th, the price of U. S. Steel was recorded in the Downward Trend column in red ink, being a new price in that column.",
   "dateRefs": [
    "1938-09-24"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "On September 29th, prices of U. S. Steel and Bethlehem Steel were recorded in the Secondary Rally column. Refer to Explanatory Rule 6-G.",
   "ruleRefs": [
    "6-G"
   ],
   "dateRefs": [
    "1938-09-29"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "On October 5th, the price of U. S. Steel was recorded in the Upward Trend column in black ink. Refer to Explanatory Rule 5-A.",
   "ruleRefs": [
    "5-A"
   ],
   "dateRefs": [
    "1938-10-05"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "On October 8th, the price of Bethlehem Steel was recorded in the Upward Trend column in black ink. Refer to Explanatory Rule 6-D.",
   "ruleRefs": [
    "6-D"
   ],
   "dateRefs": [
    "1938-10-08"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Chart Five ledger on the RIGHT page (p.111); printed annotations on the LEFT page (p.110). Year 1938 only; sequence runs Sept 12 to Oct 24, 1938. Columns per group L-to-R: SR, NR, UT, DT, NRC, SRC; groups US, BS, KP. Ink cross-check held throughout: UT=black, DT=red, all others=blue. Every dated row with all three instruments checksum-closes KP=US+BS: 13(54 1/4+53 5/8=107 7/8), 14(52+52 1/2=104 1/2), SAT24(51 7/8+52=103 7/8), 26(51 1/8+51 1/4=102 3/8), 28(50 7/8+51=101 7/8), 29(57 1/8+57 3/4=114 7/8), 30(59 1/4+59 1/2=118 3/4), OCT1(60 1/4+60=120 1/4), 3(60 3/8+60 3/8=120 3/4), 5(62+62=124), 6(63+63=126), SAT8(64 1/4+64=128 1/4), Oct13(65 3/8+65 1/8=130 1/2), SAT22(65 7/8+67 1/2=133 3/8), 24(66+carried 67 1/2=133 1/2). US row-3 initially misread as 60 7/8; zoom confirmed 60 3/8, which closes the checksum. Row 13 US 54 1/4 sits in NATURAL REACTION (col5, blue), not UT, consistent with text that US did not enter Downward Trend until Sept 14. On Sept 14 both US and KP moved into the Downward Trend column (red ink) while BS stayed in Natural Reaction. KP entered Upward Trend on Oct 5 (124, black) though BS remained in Natural Rally (col8) until Oct 8. Header carried-forward pivots underlined in red (UT triple 63 1/4/63 1/8/126 3/8, plus US-DT 55 1/2, BS-NRC 54 5/8, KP-NRC 111 1/8). Drawn black single underlines mark rally/uptrend and downtrend pivots on rows 14, 21, 28. Empty dated rows (SEPT.12, 15, 16, SAT17, 19, 22, 23, 27, 4, 7, 10, 11, 14, SAT15, 17-21) omitted per instructions.",
